Not a good idea, pet polymorph is one of the things that makes
Nethack, Nethack.  Its nerfing in Slashem is one of its bigger
misfeatures, IMO.

There's no way to control a pet's polymorph and there's too great a
chance of getting a bad result, and even if you get something awesome,
you can't control pet behavior well enough for it to be too much of an
advantage.  Then there's the need of having to keep it near you on
level changes so it doesn't go feral and give you a rude shock later,
and sometimes it hits a level teleport trap or pit and goes feral
anyway!

Count me against.

